{
  "id": 19,
  "name": "cluster_aware_return_regret",
  "intent": "Extend parent's return-aware, regret-modulated construction with a bounded cluster_density bonus that decays with progress. Early game, candidates inside dense unvisited neighborhoods gain priority, reducing stranding risk; late game, the bonus halves but persists to preserve spatial coherence during closure. Cluster_density is normalized to [0,1] so the term is bounded at 0.06, well below the unit distance coefficient, preventing loose packing while providing ranking differentiation when raw distance values are close. The seed's nearest-neighbor backbone (-d) remains dominant across all candidates.",
  "tags": [
    "cluster",
    "hybrid"
  ],
  "code": "def priority(f):\n    d = f['distance']\n    rd = f['return_distance']\n    p = f['progress']\n    reg = f['regret']\n    nr = f['nearest_remaining']\n    cd = f['cluster_density']\n    return -d + 0.25 * (1 + p) * rd + 0.15 * (1 - p) * reg - 0.12 * nr + 0.06 * (1 - 0.5 * p) * cd",
